+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] ["math" "(2x+3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] ["math" "(2x+3{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] ["math" "(3{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] ["math" "({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}x+(2x+3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2x+3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{y}^{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2y\\,\\text{d}y}{x+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-37307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\,\\text{d}x}{x+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{2\\,\\text{d}y}{x+{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2y\\,\\text{d}y}{x+{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y\\,\\text{d}y}{x+{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\,\\text{d}x}{x+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2y\\,\\text{d}y}{x+{y}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2y\\,\\text{d}y}{x+{y}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a cylinder, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the cylinder if the radius is $r=2$ and the height is $h=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the cylinder is $V=\\pi {r}^{2}h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =2\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=2$ and $h=4,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(2,4) & =2\\pi \\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =16\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-37308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16\\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "16\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\pi \\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "4\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+16\\pi \\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "4\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+\\pi \\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "8\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+2\\pi \\,\\text{d}h"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\pi \\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular solid if the lengths of the sides are $a=2,$ $b=5,$ and $c=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the rectangular solid is $V=abc.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂V}{∂c})\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =bc\\,\\text{d}a+ac\\,\\text{d}b+ab\\,\\text{d}c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=2,$ $b=5,$ and $c=1,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(2,5,1) & =5\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}a+2\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}b+5\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{d}a+5\\,\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "4\\,\\text{d}a+10\\,\\text{d}b+2\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "4\\,\\text{d}a+5\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{d}a+25\\,\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangular pyramid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular pyramid if the base is a square with the side of $a=6$ and the height is $h=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the rectangular pyramid is $V=\\frac{1}{3}{a}^{2}h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2ah}{3}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{{a}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=6$ and $h=5,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,5) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 6\\cdot 5}{3}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{{6}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =20\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{d}a+15\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "20\\,\\text{d}a+10\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "20\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "30\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "30\\,\\text{d}a+15\\,\\text{d}h"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a right cone, find the differential $\\text{d}l$ for the slant height $l$ of the right cone if its base radius is $r=3$ and height $h=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The slant height of the right cone is $l=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}l(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂l}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂l}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=3$  and $h=4$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(3,4) & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{3}{10}\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{10}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a sector of a circle, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ if the radius is $r=4$ and the central angle is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the sector is $S=\\frac{\\theta }{2}{r}^{2}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(r,\\theta ) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂S}{∂\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =r\\theta \\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(4,\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}r+8\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}r+8\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}r+8\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz),$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(1,1,1)$ to $(2,3,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y+\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,1,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(1,1,1) & =1\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y+1\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,1+Δy,1+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈Δx+Δy+Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(1,1,1)$ to $(2,3,4),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-1=1, \\\\ Δy & =3-1=2 \\\\ Δz & =4-1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈Δx+Δy+Δz \\\\  & ≈1+2+3 \\\\  & ≈6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ increases by approximately $6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-167168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=xy+x{e}^{y},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(2,0)$ to $(1,-0.5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(y+{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}x+(x+x{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(2,0) & =(0+{e}^{0})\\,\\text{d}x+(2+2\\cdot {e}^{0})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+4\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈1\\,Δx+4\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(2,0)$ to $(1,-0.5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-2=-1, \\\\ Δy & =-0.5-0=-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+4\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (-0.5) \\\\  & ≈-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ decreases by approximately $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+\\sqrt{y},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(0,4)$ to $(-1,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2xy\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,4),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(0,4) & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x+({0}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,4+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(0,4)$ to $(-1,5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =-1-0=-1, \\\\ Δy & =5-4=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈0\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $0.25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.25"] ["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "0.25"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1.25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $(0,1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,\\text{d}y-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)\\,\\text{d}x+(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\,\\text{d}y-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y+0\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,0+Δy,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy+0\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $(0,1,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =0-1=-1, \\\\ Δy & =1-0=1 \\\\ Δz & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy+0\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (1)+0\\cdot (1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ≈1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ increases by approximately $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\pi -2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{2y-z},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(-1,2,3)$ to $(1,0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={e}^{2y-z}\\,\\text{d}x+2x{e}^{2y-z}\\,\\text{d}y-x{e}^{2y-z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(-1,2,3),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(-1,2,3) & ={e}^{2(2)-3}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot {e}^{2(2)-3}\\,\\text{d}y-(-1)\\cdot {e}^{2(2)-3}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =e\\,\\text{d}x-2e\\,\\text{d}y+e\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(-1+Δx,2+Δy,3+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈e\\,Δx-2e\\,Δy+e\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(-1,2,3)$ to $(1,0,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-(-1)=2, \\\\ Δy & =0-2=-2 \\\\ Δz & =1-3=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈e\\,Δx-2e\\,Δy+e\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈e\\cdot (2)-2e\\cdot (-2)+e\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ≈4e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ increases by approximately $4e.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-167166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2e"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2e"] ["math" "4e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4e"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sqrt[3]{10}+\\sqrt{150}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{x}+\\sqrt{y}$ at the point $(8,144).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{x}^{2/3}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(8,144),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot {8}^{2/3}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{144}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{24}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(8+Δx,144+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{12}\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{24}\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{10}+\\sqrt{150}=f(10,150),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(10,150).$\n\nMoving from $(8,144)$ to $(10,150),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =10-8=2, \\\\ Δy & =150-144=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{12}(2)+\\frac{1}{24}(6) \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{5}{12} \\\\  & ≈0.417.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.417.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,150) & ≈f(8,144)+0.417 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{10}+\\sqrt{150} & ≈\\sqrt[3]{8}+\\sqrt{144}+0.417 \\\\  & ≈2+12+0.417 \\\\  & ≈14.417.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-37281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10.235"] ["math" "11.215"] ["math" "14.417"] ["math" "15.873"] ["math" "18.556"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-37281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14.417"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sqrt{{e}^{0.2}+0.1}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y}$ at the point $(0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{0}+0}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{0}+0}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{2}\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{2}\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{e}^{0.2}+0.1}=f(0.2,0.1),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(0.2,0.1).$\n\nMoving from $(0,0)$ to $(0.2,0.1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =0.2-0=0.2, \\\\ Δy & =0.1-0=0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)+\\frac{1}{2}(0.1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.05 \\\\  & =0.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.15.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.2,0.1) & ≈f(0,0)+0.15 \\\\ \\sqrt{{e}^{0.2}+0.1} & ≈\\sqrt{{e}^{0}+0}+0.15 \\\\  & =1+0.15 \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-167170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.15"] ["math" "0.25"] ["math" "1.15"] ["math" "1.18"] ["math" "1.25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $(1.81)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.91)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $(2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{2}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+2\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n(1.81)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.91)=f(1.81,0.91),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(1.81,0.91).$\n\nMoving from $(2,1)$ to $(1.81,0.91),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1.81-2=-0.19, \\\\ Δy & =0.91-1=-0.09.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (-0.19)+2\\cdot (-0.09) \\\\  & ≈0-0.18 \\\\  & ≈-0.18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $0.18.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.81,0.91) & ≈f(2,1)-0.18 \\\\ (1.81)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.91) & ≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-0.18 \\\\  & ≈0-0.18 \\\\  & ≈-0.18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.15"] ["math" "-0.16"] ["math" "-0.18"] ["math" "-0.19"] ["math" "-0.20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sqrt{4.1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.9)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $(4,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δx+1\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4.1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.9)=f(4.1,0.9),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(4.1,0.9).$\n\nMoving from $(4,1)$ to $(4.1,0.9),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =4.1-4=0.1, \\\\ Δy & =0.9-1=-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (0.1)+1(-0.1) \\\\  & ≈0.025-0.1 \\\\  & ≈-0.075.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $0.075.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4.1,0.9) & ≈f(4,1)-0.075 \\\\ \\sqrt{4.1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.9) & ≈\\sqrt{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-0.075 \\\\  & ≈2-0.075 \\\\  & ≈1.925.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.910"] ["math" "1.915"] ["math" "1.920"] ["math" "1.925"] ["math" "1.930"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.925"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)$ at the point $({\\pi }^{2},0).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $({\\pi }^{2},0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x-\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $({\\pi }^{2}+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,Δx-\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2)=f({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $({\\pi }^{2},0)$ to $({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =({\\pi }^{2}+1)-{\\pi }^{2}=1, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈(-\\frac{1}{2\\pi })\\cdot (1)-1\\cdot (0.2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }-0.2 \\\\  & ≈-0.359.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $-0.359.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2) & ≈f({\\pi }^{2},0)-0.359 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}+0)-0.359 \\\\  & =0-0.359 \\\\  & =-0.359.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.274"] ["math" "-0.359"] ["math" "-0.482"] ["math" "-0.521"] ["math" "-0.652"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.359"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d87ed6768b1ac7be0005d61d94f675f7dc8b308097c7536bf478982ab815634"} {"question" "e-6852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the differential for $f(x,y) = x^2 \\sin y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6852.json" "file_sha256" "8f4eaebc4cefa1e364a0614d88b75fe4a71ad98ef12a8bd09273bf4c44c28a32"} {"question" "e-6852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6852.json" "file_sha256" "8f4eaebc4cefa1e364a0614d88b75fe4a71ad98ef12a8bd09273bf4c44c28a32"} {"question" "e-6854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a cone, find the differential $\\textrm d V$ for the volume $V$ of the cone if the radius is $r=6$ and the height is $h = 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6854.json" "file_sha256" "e3472bb45ef822d35a054ec8b4b5e1a02cbd63d184ffe41d78afc32a09d60467"} {"question" "e-6854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the cone is $V = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\pi r^2h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6$ and $h=3,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3) & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi \\cdot 6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi \\cdot {6}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =12\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+12\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6854.json" "file_sha256" "e3472bb45ef822d35a054ec8b4b5e1a02cbd63d184ffe41d78afc32a09d60467"} {"question" "e-6875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f (x, y) = xe^y ,$ use the differential $\\textrm d f$ to estimate the change $\\Delta f$ in the value of $f(x, y)$ from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6875.json" "file_sha256" "d28f9ddbbb5ccdbe634b248c7433d02541277fff3bcbe16b9d18802e1968eb29"} {"question" "e-6875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(5,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(5,0) & ={e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x+5{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+5\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(5 + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx 1 \\, \\Delta x + 5 \\, \\Delta y.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-5=-3, \\\\ Δy & =1-0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+5\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6875.json" "file_sha256" "d28f9ddbbb5ccdbe634b248c7433d02541277fff3bcbe16b9d18802e1968eb29"} {"question" "e-6876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)$ using a differential of the function $f(x,y) = \\sin x + \\cos y$ at the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6876.json" "file_sha256" "3afaf863ff89565d3ad90a89a700970d12a90e615a7a7403c5a4c09c4fc11865"} {"question" "e-6876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-1\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\pi + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx  -1  \\,  \\Delta x + 0  \\,  \\Delta y\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)= f(3,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $(\\pi, 0)$ to $(3,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3-\\pi ≈-0.141, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈-1(-0.141)+0(0.2) \\\\  & ≈0.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,0.2) & ≈f(\\pi ,0)+0.141 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0.141 \\\\  & ≈0+1+0.141 \\\\  & ≈1.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6876.json" "file_sha256" "3afaf863ff89565d3ad90a89a700970d12a90e615a7a7403c5a4c09c4fc11865"}] "usage" {"q-37307" [] "q-37281" [] "q-37295" [] "q-37308" [] "q-79837" [] "e-6852" [] "e-6854" [] "e-6876" [] "e-6875" []} "basis" 1910 "retractions" [[17592186124972 :question/problem "Find the differential $df$ for the function $f(x, y) = \\ln (x + y^{2})$."] [17592186124973 :question/problem "Given a cylinder, find the differential $dV$ for the volume $V$ of the cylinder if the radius is $r = 2$ and the height is $h = 4$."] [17592186124969 :question/problem "Given a sector of a circle, find the differential $dS$ for the surface area $S$ if the radius is $r = 4$ and the central angle is $θ = \\frac{π}{8}$."] [17592186124967 :question/problem "Estimate $\\sqrt[3]{10} + \\sqrt{150}$ using a differential $df$ of the function $f(x, y) = \\sqrt[3]{x} + \\sqrt{y}$ at the point $(8, 144)$. Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."] [17592186125143 :question/problem "Estimate $(1.81) \\cdot \\ln (0.91)$ using a differential $df$ of the function $f(x, y) = x\\ln y$ at the point $(2, 1)$."] [17592186124292 :question/problem "Find the differential for $f(x,y) = x^2 \\sin y$."] [17592186124292 :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= (\\frac{∂f}{∂x})dx + (\\frac{∂f}{∂y})dy \\\\\n&= (2x\\sin y)dx + (x^{2}\\cos y)dy \\\\\n&= 2x\\sin ydx + x^{2}\\cos ydy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186124293 :question/problem "Given a cone, find the differential $\\textrm d V$ for the volume $V$ of the cone if the radius is $r=6$ and the height is $h = 3$."] [17592186124293 :question/worked-solution "The volume of the cone is\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\pi r^2h\n$$\n\nLet's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndV(r, h) &= (\\frac{∂V}{∂r})dr + (\\frac{∂V}{∂h})dh \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}πrhdr + \\frac{1}{3}πr^{2}dh\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6$ and $h=3$, the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndV(6, 3) &= \\frac{2}{3}π \\cdot 6 \\cdot 3dr + \\frac{1}{3}π \\cdot 6^{2}dh \\\\\n&= 12πdr + 12πdh\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186124294 :question/problem "If $f (x, y) = xe^y$, use the differential $\\textrm d f$ to estimate the change $\\Delta f$ in the value of $f(x, y)$ from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1)$."] [17592186124294 :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= (\\frac{∂f}{∂x})dx + (\\frac{∂f}{∂y})dy \\\\\n&= e^{y}dx + xe^{y}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(5,0)$, the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(5, 0) &= e^{0}dx + 5e^{0}dy \\\\\n&= 1dx + 5dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(5 + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y)$, then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx 1 \\, \\Delta x + 5 \\, \\Delta y\n$$\n\nMoving from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔx &= 2 - 5 =-3, \\\\\nΔy &= 1 - 0 = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nΔf \\mid \\approx 1Δx + 5Δy; \\approx 1 \\cdot (-3) + 5 \\cdot (1); \\approx 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $2$."] [17592186124295 :question/problem "Estimate $\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)$ using a differential of the function $f(x,y) = \\sin x + \\cos y$ at the point $\\left(\\pi, 0 \\right)$."] [17592186124295 :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= (\\frac{∂f}{∂x})dx + (\\frac{∂f}{∂y})dy \\\\\n&= \\cos xdx - \\sin ydy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point\n\n$$\n\\left(\\pi, 0 \\right)\n$$\n\nthe differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= \\cos πdx - \\sin 0dy \\\\\n&=-1dx + 0dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\pi + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y)$, then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx -1 \\, \\Delta x + 0 \\, \\Delta y\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)= f(3,0.2)\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3,0.2)$.\n\nMoving from $(\\pi, 0)$ to $(3,0.2)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔx &= 3 - π \\approx - 0.141, \\\\\nΔy &= 0.2 - 0 = 0.2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nΔf \\mid \\approx - 1(-0.141) + 0(0.2); \\approx 0.141\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141$. Consequently, we have\n\n$$\nf(3, 0.2)\\begin{vmatrix}\\approx f(π, 0) + 0.141 \\\\ \\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)\\end{vmatrix}\\approx \\sin (π) + \\cos (0) + 0.141; \\approx 0 + 1 + 0.141; \\approx 1.141\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186122825 17592186122826 17592186122827 17592186122828 17592186122829 17592186122837 17592186122838 17592186122839 17592186122840 17592186122841 17592186122855 17592186122856 17592186122857 17592186122858 17592186122859 17592186122861 17592186122862 17592186122863 17592186122864 17592186122865 17592186123881 17592186123882 17592186123883 17592186123884 17592186123885] "immutable_fields" [[17592186122824 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122824 :answer-field/id] [17592186122824 :answer-field/key] [17592186122824 :answer-field/type] [17592186122836 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122836 :answer-field/id] [17592186122836 :answer-field/key] [17592186122836 :answer-field/type] [17592186122854 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122854 :answer-field/id] [17592186122854 :answer-field/key] [17592186122854 :answer-field/type] [17592186122860 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122860 :answer-field/id] [17592186122860 :answer-field/key] [17592186122860 :answer-field/type] [17592186123880 :answer-field/correct] [17592186123880 :answer-field/id] [17592186123880 :answer-field/key] [17592186123880 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
